hero# Doctor
 desc# A single-file documentation language that compiles to clean HTML. No terminal. No dependencies. Just write and deploy.

h2# What is Doctor?

p# **Doctor** is a markup language designed for one purpose: creating beautiful documentation sites with zero friction. You write `.doctor` files, push them to GitHub, and they automatically compile to responsive HTML with dark mode support.

alert#tip
 p# This entire page was written in Doctor. You are looking at the output right now.

h2# Quick Start

p# You can have a live docs site in under 5 minutes without ever opening a terminal:

list#
- **Fork** the Doctor template repository on GitHub
- **Edit** `.doctor` files in the `docs/` folder directly on GitHub
- **Commit** your changes — GitHub Actions auto-compiles and deploys
- **Your site is live** at `yourname.github.io/doctor`
end#

grid#3
card# Fork & Edit
 desc# Fork the template repo and edit .doctor files right on GitHub.
card# Push & Build
 desc# Every commit triggers GitHub Actions to compile your docs automatically.
card# Live & Done
 desc# Your site is live at yourname.github.io/repo in under a minute.
end#

h2# Syntax Guide

p# Doctor is **line-based**. Every component starts with a name followed by `#`, then content. Multi-line blocks close with `end#`.

code#doctor
// This is a comment
title# My Documentation

hero# Welcome
 desc# This is my docs site.

h2# Getting Started
p# Write docs in **Doctor** and deploy to GitHub Pages.

code#python
def hello():
    return "Hello, Doctor!"
end#
end#

h2# Components

table# Component | Syntax | Description
 title | title# Name | Sets the page title
 nav | nav# Label | #href | Top navigation link
 sidebar | sidebar# Label | #href | Left sidebar link
 hero | hero# Title + desc# | Large header section
 heading | h1# h2# h3# | Section headers with anchors
 paragraph | p# Text | Body with **bold**, *italic*, `code`
 code | code#lang ... end# | Syntax-highlighted code
 table | table# Cols... end# | Styled data tables
 list | list# ... end# | Bullet lists
 alert | alert#type + p# | Info, warning, success, error, tip
 card | card# Title + desc# | Info cards
 grid | grid#N ... end# | Responsive card layouts
 divider | divider# | Horizontal rule
 image | img# src | alt | Responsive images
end#

h3# Headings

p# Use `h1#`, `h2#`, and `h3#` for section headings. They automatically get anchor IDs for sidebar linking:

code#doctor
h1# Main Title
h2# Section Heading
h3# Subsection
end#

h3# Paragraphs

p# The `p#` component supports inline Markdown formatting:

code#doctor
p# This is **bold text**, *italic text*, and `inline code`.
p# You can also add [links](https://example.com).
end#

h3# Code Blocks

p# Use `code#` followed by the language, then your code, then `end#`:

code#javascript
// Fetch user data from the API
async function getUser(id) {
    const response = await fetch(`/api/users/${id}`);
    if (!response.ok) {
        throw new Error('User not found');
    }
    return response.json();
}
end#

h3# Tables

p# Pipe-separated columns. First line is headers, subsequent lines are rows:

code#doctor
table# Feature | Status | Version
 Dark mode | Done | v1.0
 Mobile layout | Done | v1.0
 Search | Planned | v2.0
end#

h3# Alerts

p# Five types with distinct colors and icons:

code#doctor
alert#info
 p# This is an info callout.

alert#warning
 p# Be careful with this step.

alert#success
 p# Operation completed successfully.

alert#error
 p# Something went wrong.

alert#tip
 p# Pro tip: you can combine multiple alerts.
end#

h3# Lists

p# Dash-prefixed items inside a `list#` block:

code#doctor
list#
- No dependencies to install
- Works on any device with a browser
- Auto-deploys on every commit
- Dark mode included
end#

h3# Cards and Grids

p# Cards are info boxes. Grids arrange them in columns (2, 3, or 4):

code#doctor
grid#3
card# Fast
 desc# Compiles in milliseconds.
card# Clean
 desc# Semantic HTML output.
card# Portable
 desc# One file, works everywhere.
end#

h2# Tips

list#
- **Comments** start with `//` and are ignored by the compiler
- **Indentation** does not matter — Doctor is line-based
- **Empty lines** between components are optional but improve readability
- **Every** multi-line block must end with `end#` or the compiler will break
- **Sidebar links** should match heading anchors (auto-generated from heading text)
end#

alert#warning
 p# The most common mistake is forgetting to close a block with `end#`. Always check your `code#`, `table#`, `list#`, and `grid#` blocks.

divider#

p# Ready to start? Edit `docs/index.doctor` in your repo and replace this content with your own documentation.

p# Made with [Doctor](https://github.com). Deployed on [GitHub Pages](https://pages.github.com).
